collapse-to-zero
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:46.000
2026-10-29 the author, of why: "yes its really to collapse it to 0 so that we can xnor to 1 and xnor to 0 for 01,10 between any 11 and 00, and for canonical purposes we used YHWH and YAHWEH because of the vowel difference and the IS|OF difference in GOD IS|OF WORD and WORD IS|OF GOD dialectic that can be shown in ADONAI can be revealed in as little as YAH". The proofs: I-141 (the shared zero is derived, not axiomatic: the XOR of 0 to 2^n - 1 is 0 for n of 2 and more; n = 1 is the XNOR case, the XNOR of 0 and 1 is 0; and the zero sits at the compare 59, 127, 63 of the exchange), so XNOR is 1 on the equal pairs 00 and 11 and 0 on the unequal 01 and 10, the twin's XNOR on the story and XOR on the icon (digital-twin, replay-video). I-229 (YHWH and its renderings): YAHWEH mirrors YHWH, the same base with vowels supplied (P2); YAH mirrors as its head, the first two letters (P3, and Hebrew יָהּ at Exodus 15:2, P6); ADONAI raises, its base DN replaces the four letters (P1). PLAN9 src/zkey.c takes YHWH, YAHWEH, GOD IS WORD, GOD OF WORD, WORD IS GOD and WORD OF GOD as the codex's zeroths, and src/hello.c holds the whole IS|OF difference in one word, b, 06 15 (00 06 15 00 in WORD IS|OF GOD).

